  "asr_text": "I stood still for an hour. Imagine such control! He remained awake, listening. Once he gave a small groan of terror. I knew that sound from my own sleepless nights. At last, I opened the lantern a little. The ray fell upon the eye, wide open. Then I heard his heart, a low, quick beat, like a watch wrapped in cotton. It grew faster, louder. Surely a neighbor would hear! I rushed in. He shrieked once before I dragged him down and pulled the heavy bed over him. Soon the beating stopped. I checked. He was dead. I hid his body beneath three floorboards and replaced them perfectly. No stain, no mark. Would a madman have worked so neatly?",
